    rationale: { body: "Float assignments are ethical when the nurse is given an orientation, paired with an experienced staff member if needed, and assigned tasks within their competency. Refusing entirely can be classified as patient abandonment; performing tasks outside competency is unsafe. Negotiate scope-appropriate work.", sources: [NCSBN_RN_PLAN, { label: "ANA — Position Statement on Floating" }] },
